{"items":[{"id":"cap-v2-replacement-ordering_and_selection-typescript-repair-01","problem":"Repair the TypeScript implementation below and return one complete source file.

Implement exactly this public API:

```ts
export interface RestockCandidate {
  sku: string;
  urgency: number;
  onHand: number;
}

export function selectRestocks(
  lines: readonly string[],
  limit: number,
): RestockCandidate[];
```

Each input line must have the exact form `SKU,urgency,onHand`:

- `SKU` must match `[A-Z][A-Z0-9]{1,7}`.
- `urgency` must be one decimal digit from `0` through `9`.
- `onHand` must be a canonical non-negative decimal integer: either `0` or a digit from `1` through `9` followed by zero or more digits. Its parsed value must be a safe integer.
- Whitespace, missing or extra fields, signs, decimal points, and any other deviations make the entire line malformed.
- Malformed lines are ignored.
- If `limit` is not a non-negative safe integer, return an empty array.

Rank valid candidates by higher urgency first, then lower `onHand`, then earlier position in the original `lines` array. Return at most `limit` candidates. Preserve duplicate valid lines as separate candidates. Do not mutate `lines`.

Do not use the filesystem, network, clock, randomness, external packages, or frameworks. Do not export anything other than the specified interface and function.

The following source has one semantic defect. Correct it:

```ts
export interface RestockCandidate {
  sku: string;
  urgency: number;
  onHand: number;
}

type IndexedCandidate = RestockCandidate & { index: number };

const LINE_PATTERN = /^([A-Z][A-Z0-9]{1,7}),([0-9]),(0|[1-9][0-9]*)$/;

export function selectRestocks(
  lines: readonly string[],
  limit: number,
): RestockCandidate[] {
  if (!Number.isSafeInteger(limit) || limit < 0) {
    return [];
  }

  const candidates: IndexedCandidate[] = [];

  for (let index = 0; index < lines.length; index += 1) {
    const match = LINE_PATTERN.exec(lines[index]);
    if (match === null) {
      continue;
    }

    const urgency = Number(match[2]);
    const onHand = Number(match[3]);
    if (!Number.isSafeInteger(onHand)) {
      continue;
    }

    candidates.push({ sku: match[1], urgency, onHand, index });
  }

  candidates.sort((left, right) => {
    if (left.urgency !== right.urgency) {
      return right.urgency - left.urgency;
    }
    if (left.onHand !== right.onHand) {
      return left.onHand - right.onHand;
    }
    if (left.sku < right.sku) {
      return -1;
    }
    if (left.sku > right.sku) {
      return 1;
    }
    return 0;
  });

  return candidates.slice(0, limit).map(({ sku, urgency, onHand }) => ({
    sku,
    urgency,
    onHand,
  }));
}
